Sure, I can help you create a simple, minimalist homepage with placeholder navigation links for your future experiments. Below is a basic HTML structure with some CSS to achieve a light, clean, and minimalist design. This will include placeholders for a home page, calculator, tarot deck simulator, weather app, and pong game.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Minimalist Homepage</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
            color: #333;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            height: 100vh;
        }

        nav {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        ul {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding: 0;
        }

        li {
            display: inline;
            margin: 0 15px;
        }

        a {
            text-decoration: none;
            color: #333;
            font-weight: bold;
            transition: color 0.3s;
        }

        a:hover {
            color: #007BFF;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 2.5em;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to SpiritOS</h1>
    <nav>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Calculator</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Tarot Deck Simulator</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Weather App</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Pong</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    <p>This is a minimalist homepage for future experiments.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: The HTML includes a `nav` element with an unordered list (`ul`) containing list items (`li`) for each of the placeholder links.
- **CSS Styling**: 
  - The body is styled to be centered and uses a light background color.
  - The navigation links are styled to be inline, with some margin for spacing.
  - Links change color on hover for a simple interactive effect.
  - The font is set to Arial for a clean look, and the color scheme is kept minimal with shades of gray and blue for hover effects.

This setup provides a basic framework for your homepage, and you can expand upon it as you develop each of the individual applications.
